e general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Bill Huizenga (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Southwest Michigan's 4th District is one of the House's closest contests. Incumbent Bill Huizenga, a Republican in an R+3 seat, faces Democratic nominee Sean McCann in a race shaped by a strong Democratic national environment. Huizenga has a fundraising edge and incumbent advantages, but outside groups have spent heavily against him while McCann has drawn support from groups like GIFFORDS PAC.\n\nExpert ratings are divided: several call it a Tossup, most others Lean R, and one rates it Lean D for a flip. Prediction markets give Huizenga a modest edge near 53-54 percent. With no reliable general-election polling, the race rests on fundamentals and expert judgment, pointing to a narrow Republican advantage with wide uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5309, "margin": 0.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4667, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4711, "margin": -1.0}]}